# The folder chip's menu and peek: a right click on the chip = Copy Name /
# Copy Path / Open in Finder (Copy flashes the chip); its peek (no copy
# button): a click on the path copies it and the path flashes (no hover
# expand until the mouse leaves), a right click = the same menu, the mouse
# resting on it expands it; its last row (the current folder) copies the path. Run with GTTY_SHOW_DRY=1 in a scratch folder:
#   mkdir -p w && cd w && GTTY_SHOW_DRY=1 gtty --script $REPO/test/folderchip.gt
# Shots go to the folder above.
/s bash
/wait 1500
/rclick 45 620
/wait 400
/shot ../fc1-menu.bmp
/click 80 640
/wait 100
/shot ../fc2-copied-name.bmp
/wait 500
/rclick 45 620
/wait 300
/click 80 698
/wait 400
/shot ../fc3-open.bmp
/pace 100
/move 45 620
/wait 500
/shot ../fc4-peek.bmp
/click 300 612
/shot ../fc5-copy-flash.bmp
/wait 800
/shot ../fc5b-still-folded.bmp
/pace 400
/rclick 300 612
/wait 300
/shot ../fc6-peek-menu.bmp
/key escape
/wait 300
/move 45 620
/wait 1400
/shot ../fc7-expanded.bmp
/click 300 609
/shot ../fc8-current-copied.bmp
/quit
